# =====================================================================
# Trivy risk acceptances for the keycloak image
# =====================================================================
# Every entry needs: the reason it does not affect us, who accepted it,
# and an expiry date (exp:). After that date Trivy reports it again and
# the pipeline fails until someone fixes it or re-accepts it.
#
# Accepted 2026-10-23 (pending instructor review)
# Short expiry on purpose: re-check when Keycloak publishes a new 26.x
# patch image (bump the FROM lines in the Dockerfile and rescan).
# =====================================================================

# --- OS packages in the upstream ubi9-micro base image ---------------
# The Keycloak image has no package manager, so these cannot be patched
# in our Dockerfile; they are fixed when Keycloak rebuilds its image.

# ca-certificates (CA trust store update)
CVE-2026-114406 exp:2026-11-30

# pcre2 / pcre2-syntax (regular-expression library)
CVE-2026-103111 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-86145 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-89161 exp:2026-11-30

# --- Bundled JDBC driver that CredPay never loads --------------------
# mssql-jdbc ships with Keycloak for SQL Server users. CredPay is built
# with KC_DB=postgres (Dockerfile), so the SQL Server driver is not used.
CVE-2025-59250 exp:2027-01-31
